    "created_at": "2019-01-08T21:41:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-08T21:41:50Z",
    "body": "Hi gregjhogan,\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, WebUSB on shared workers in Chrome is not going to be implemented anytime soon because the future of shared workers is uncertain. See [https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/315](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/315) for some context.\r\n\r\nThere is an [intent to implement and ship the throttling of background dedicated workers](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!topic/blink-dev/8xpEA-iNHwg), which will throttle dedicated workers by default. However, there is a proposal to allow users to opt-out of the throttling (see the [design doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fgk-jMjwucb7kKz4zcMnBG1qKJ6edq6PTylZAgZEDY0/edit#)). This could potentially solve your problem with the process becoming suspended when switching tabs.\r\n\r\nPlease file a bug at [https://crbug.com](https://crbug.com) with the Blink>USB component so that we can track the issue.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
