    "created_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:41Z",
    "body": "One detail has changed since the older throttling discussion here: current Chromium explicitly registers an opened WebUSB device with the scheduler using `DisableAggressiveThrottling()`.\n\nThat doesn't solve multi-tab ownership, but it weakens the original motivation that a Dedicated Worker necessarily becomes unsuitable when its tab backgrounds.\n\nIt might be worth benchmarking the modern Dedicated Worker + Web Locks/BroadcastChannel design before adding another exposure surface specifically for scheduling reasons.\n",
